  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "The total area of all the faces of a rectangular solid is \\(22\\text{ cm}^2,\\) and the total length of all its edges is \\(24\\text{ cm}.\\) Then the length in cm of any one of its internal diagonals is",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\sqrt{11}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\sqrt{12}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\sqrt{13}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\sqrt{14}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "not uniquely determined"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1984-p25.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The conditions give \\(2(xy+xz+yz)=22\\) and \\(4(x+y+z)=24,\\) so \\(xy+xz+yz=11\\) and \\(x+y+z=6.\\) Hence the square of an internal diagonal is \\[ x^2+y^2+z^2=6^2-2(11)=14. \\] Its length is \\(\\sqrt{14}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Let the side lengths be \\(x,y,z\\) and translate both totals into equations",
        "Expand \\((x+y+z)^2\\) to find \\(x^2+y^2+z^2\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
